Package: tidyinvasion
Title: Tidy Tools for Invasion Biology
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Jimmy", "Moses", , "jimmy.moses@pnguot.ac.pg", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3342-2384"))
Description: Pipe-friendly tools for the quantitative study of biological
    invasions, from introduction to impact. Covers propagule pressure and
    establishment dose-response models (Leung et al. 2004
    <doi:10.1890/02-0571>), imperfect detection with single-season
    occupancy models, rates of
    spatial spread, dispersal kernels and lag phases, Skellam
    reaction-diffusion spread, the Environmental Impact Classification for
    Alien Taxa (Blackburn et al. 2014 <doi:10.1371/journal.pbio.1001850>),
    biotic homogenisation, eradication feasibility and horizon scanning.
    Species distribution modelling is supported through 'tidymodels'
    extensions: 'recipes' steps for background sampling, lagged propagule
    pressure and environmental novelty, 'rsample' spatial block and temporal
    transfer resampling, 'yardstick' metrics (Continuous Boyce Index and
    True Skill Statistic) and 'parsnip' model specifications. Data frames
    and 'sf' point layers are accepted, distances and likelihoods are
    computed in base R, and results are returned as tibbles.
